  "preamble": "The clearest diachronic depalatalization of /ɡʲ/ is the centum merger: the Proto-Indo-European palatovelar *ǵ, usually interpreted as a palatalized velar [ɡʲ], merged with plain *g in the centum branches (Italic, Hellenic, Celtic, Germanic, Anatolian, Tocharian), while satem branches turned it into sibilants or affricates. Synchronic alternations such as Russian noga [ɡ] ~ nogi [ɡʲ] are automatic allophony before front vowels, not a sound change.",
  "phoneticEffects": "Depalatalization, Merger",
